<title>HONG KONG: China Resources 1996 net rises 109 pct.</title>
<headline>China Resources 1996 net rises 109 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   49.0 vs 26.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    8.0 vs 6.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  203.55 vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    596.67 vs 284.93</p>
<p>    Turnover		     1,961.88 vs 1,605.06</p>
<p>    Company name		 China Resources Enterprise Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  June 12</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   July 3</p>
<p>NOTE - China Resources operates cold storage, brewery and property businesses.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain of HK$203.55 million linked to the floation of China Resources subsidiary China Resources Beijing Land Ltd in November 1996.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 11.0 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of three cents) vs eight cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
